    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d143">

                <pb facs="0320" n="248" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg248"/>

                <head>No. 18.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Earl Granville to Mr. Lowell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-12-30"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 30,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of the 23d instant, requesting, on behalf of your government, to
                    be informed as to the grounds upon which Denis H. O’Connor was arrested and
                    imprisoned by the British authorities in Ireland; and I have the honor to
                    acquairt you, in reply, that I have referred your application to the proper
                    department of Her Majesty’s Government.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GRANVILLE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
